# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the real .env.
#
# Credentials only. Everything describing how OJ behaves lives in
# oj-config.yaml, which is safe to commit and meant to be reviewed as a diff.
#
# Whatever is set here is held by OJO and by OJO alone. It is never placed in a
# worker's environment, never written into a clone's .git/config, and never
# passed on a command line — see workerEnv() in src/worker.ts, which builds the
# worker's environment from an allowlist and then checks the result against the
# live token before spawning.

# ── GitHub App (preferred) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set all three, or none. A partial configuration is a startup error rather
# than a silent fallback to the PAT below — a typo'd installation id should not
# quietly result in a month of reviews posted under a human's name.
#
# Why the App is preferred:
#   - installation tokens expire in an hour, so a leaked one has a short life
#   - permissions are per-repository, granted by installing rather than by
#     trusting whoever holds the string
#   - reviews are attributed to the app, not to a person who did not write them
#   - 5000 requests/hour of its own, not shared with your account
#
# Required permissions (Repository):
#   Contents        Read-only    clone the PR head and read OJ.md from the base
#   Pull requests   Read & write post reviews, comments, and remove the label
#   Metadata        Read-only    mandatory, granted automatically
#
# Nothing else. In particular OJ never needs write access to Contents — it does
# not push, and an app that cannot push is an app that cannot be made to push.
#
# See SETUP.md § Creating the GitHub App for the walkthrough.
# OJ_GITHUB_APP_ID=
# OJ_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID=
# OJ_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/etc/oj/oj-app.private-key.pem

# ── Personal access token (quick start) ───────────────────────────────────
# A fallback so you can watch a repo in five minutes. Use a FINE-GRAINED token
# scoped to exactly the repositories you want reviewed:
#   github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
#   Repository permissions: Contents read, Pull requests read+write.
#
# The costs, stated plainly: it does not expire unless you make it, it carries
# your identity so every review reads as though you wrote it, and its rate
# limit is shared with everything else you do with that account.
#
# GITHUB_TOKEN is also read, for compatibility with the usual name.
# OJ_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ── Anthropic ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL, and usually omitted.
#
# Workers are Claude Code sessions and authenticate the way the `claude` CLI
# does for the user running this service: an ANTHROPIC_API_KEY if one is
# exported, otherwise the OAuth credentials in that user's home directory.
# Leave this unset to run on an existing Claude subscription — which is also
# why the workers are not spawned with --bare, since that flag refuses to read
# OAuth at all.
#
# The service must therefore run as a user who has actually logged in. See
# SETUP.md § Authentication.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Config location ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to ./oj-config.yaml relative to the working directory.
# OJ_CONFIG_PATH=/home/npurcell/oj/oj-config.yaml
